[2020-01-21T11:26:44Z | pierantoniomerlino | comment]
As done in the [Eddystone Driver](https://github.com/eclipse/kura/blob/develop/kura/org.eclipse.kura.driver.eddystone.provider/src/main/java/org/eclipse/kura/internal/driver/eddystone/EddystoneDriver.java), if a driver doesn't support read operation, the `read` method should return an empty `ChannelRecord`, setting the status to failed:

```
    @Override
    public void read(final List<ChannelRecord> records) throws ConnectionException {
        logger.warn(READ_ERROR_MESSAGE);
        for (final ChannelRecord record : records) {
            record.setChannelStatus(new ChannelStatus(FAILURE, READ_ERROR_MESSAGE, null));
            record.setTimestamp(System.currentTimeMillis());
        }
    }
```

Moreover, the `PreparedRead` method should return null:

```
    @Override
    public PreparedRead prepareRead(List<ChannelRecord> channelRecords) {
        logger.warn(READ_ERROR_MESSAGE);
        return null;
    }
```

In this way, no exceptions are thrown and the channels are correctly displayed in the web UI.

