This  "retryLogic->retryTimeoutLimitInSeconds" variable controls the limit to stop retry. A limit to stop retry is different from the "interval" (delay) to next retry.  In your case 1, you said there's a way to set a reasonable value to retry timeout limit, but for IoT device, we don't want to stop retry, we want the retry continue and retry should happen in an expected/predicable way until network resumed. We would like the retry policy to provide a way for us to set a retry interval, not a TIMEOUT TO STOP RETRY.

